	(text
		"ADS1235 SUPPLIES, SPI3 AND CONTROL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 67.31 122.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eae90a7a-8216-5c37-abc2-676f9dc0c802")
	)
	(text
		"J501 PIN-OUT - HBK S2M SIX-WIRE CABLE (data sheet B03594, 2025-02-28)\n  1 SIG+   (white)     3 EXC+   (blue)      5 SENSE- (gray)\n  2 SIG-   (red)       4 SENSE+ (green)     6 EXC-   (black)\n  7 SHLD, 8 SHLD - cable screen / drain, tied to GND through R510\nBridge 350 ohm nominal, 2 mV/V, 5 V excitation -> +/-10 mV FS, ~14.5 mA.\nOutput is positive in compression. The same terminal block accepts a\nresistive bridge simulator for bring-up step 6 of TEST_PLAN.md.\n\nDEFAULT BUILD IS 6-WIRE (DEC-0014): R506 and R507 are DNP.\nFit R506 + R507 for a 4-wire cell. That ties SENSE+/- to EXC+/- at the\nconnector, so the reference stops tracking the lead drop and the\nmeasurement loses Kelvin sensing - it is the lower-accuracy option."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1904f2c6-8851-51a4-a400-3763f4fd308b")
	)
	(text
		"OPERATING POINT (prelim calc Force sheet; ADS1235 SBAS824)\n  Gain 128, 4800 SPS, Sinc2, VREF = bridge excitation (ratiometric)\n  FSR = +/-VREF/128 = +/-39.06 mV (78.125 mV span) vs +/-10 mV signal\n  Input-referred noise 0.29 uVrms / 2.4 uVpp (data sheet table 1)\n    = 12.0 mNpp (V50N) / 2.4 mNpp (V10N) vs REQ-FF-04 20 / 5 mNpp\n  Ratiometric operation cancels excitation drift and noise, so the\n  5 V rail does not need to be a precision reference.\n\nFILTERS - the ADS1235 data sheet figure 84 reference design.\n  Signal and reference filters are deliberately identical so their\n  corner frequencies match: 100R series per leg, 1 nF C0G common mode\n  to AVSS, 10 nF C0G differential. The differential capacitor is 10x\n  the common-mode capacitors, so common-mode capacitor mismatch\n  converts little common-mode noise into differential noise.\n  Differential corner ~76 kHz, common mode ~1.6 MHz; the ADC PGA\n  antialias filter (C514, 4.7 nF C0G) is at 60 kHz.\n  R505 (100k) across the sense pair is the data sheet reference\n  monitor resistor: it collapses VREF if the cable is unplugged so\n  REFL_ALM asserts. It sits on the bridge side of R503/R504 so its\n  50 uA does not develop an error across the reference filter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d85b88a4-5864-502b-bc21-a0177e2a4c8a")
	)
	(text
		"ADS1235 PIN USE\n  AIN4 / AIN5 = SIG+ / SIG- (bridge output, PGA gain 128)\n  REFP0 / REFN0 = SENSE+ / SENSE-, external reference, ratiometric\n    (data sheet 8.3.4.2: \"for 6-wire strain-gauge bridge applications\n     that use excitation-sense connections, connect the excitation\n     sense lines to the reference input pins\")\n  AIN0..AIN3 unused - biased to AVDD through 10k (R522..R525) per\n    data sheet 9.1.3. Resistors rather than a hard tie keep the pins\n    safe if firmware ever configures them as GPIO or AC-excitation\n    outputs, which are referenced to AVDD/AVSS.\n  PWRDN tied high through R519; reset by command or by ADS1235_nRESET.\n  CAPP/CAPN 4.7 nF C0G and BYPASS 1 uF to DGND are both mandatory.\n  EP (footprint pad 33) to AVSS.\n  AVDD = +5VA (also the excitation rail), DVDD = +3V3 so the serial\n    interface sits at STM32 logic level."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 130.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6e1847fa-80d2-54be-8555-5fc82f10ef4b")
	)
	(text
		"TEST AND ISOLATION PROVISIONS (TEST_PLAN.md section 4)\n  TP501 excitation+   TP502/TP503 sense+/-   TP504/TP505 ADC reference\n  FL501/FL502 U.FL on the ADC-side SIG+/SIG- nodes - the noise-floor\n    measurement that decides REQ-FF-04. Placed symmetrically so the\n    differential pair stays balanced (TEST_PLAN section 2.3).\n  TP506..TP514 hooks on every MCU-facing net; TP515/TP516 GND hooks\n    sit in the same column for the scope ground clip.\n  R508 excitation feed link and R509 excitation return link: open\n    either to isolate the bridge, or replace one with a meter to\n    measure excitation current (isolation link and current break in\n    one part - see docs/decisions/actuator-sch-afe.md).\n  R510 ties the cable screen to GND at the connector; lift it to test\n    a floating screen.\n  R511..R518 (47R) are the ADS1235 data sheet series terminators AND\n    the SPI3 isolation links: remove one to take the ADC off the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 174.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0a87b1ff-6548-5b94-bd6a-f56986e9afac")
	)
	(text
		"CLOCK - ADS1235_CLKIN COMES FROM STM32 MCO2 (REQ-AR-09)\n  R520 fitted = MCO2 drives CLKIN. R521 (DNP) instead grounds CLKIN,\n  selecting the ADC internal 7.3728 MHz oscillator - a bring-up\n  fallback if the MCO2 clock tree is not ready. Fit one, never both.\n  FOR THE MCU / FIRMWARE TASK: the .ioc leaves MCO2PinFreq_Value at\n  the CubeMX default 64 MHz, outside the ADS1235 1..8 MHz CLKIN\n  range. The clock tree must deliver 7.3728 MHz nominal on PC9."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.19 219.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4b08c96a-03b9-513e-9f37-2517ef30844a")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
